! STP hardening - root guard, BPDU guard, UDLD, and RSTP tuning
!
! Beyond the basics: a rogue switch plugged into an access port can
! win root election. These protections stop loops at the edge instead
! of relying on convergence to recover.
!
spanning-tree mode rapid-pvst

! Pin the root bridge (priority 0 wins) so a foreign switch cannot take over
spanning-tree vlan 10 priority 0
spanning-tree vlan 20 priority 0

! Uplink interfaces: never let a loop form back toward the core
interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1
 description To-CORE-Primary
 spanning-tree guard root
!
interface GigabitEthernet1/0/2
 description To-CORE-Backup
 spanning-tree guard root

! Access ports: disable unidirectional links entirely (UDLD aggressive)
udld enable
udld aggressive
interface range GigabitEthernet1/0/3 - 24
 spanning-tree bpduguard enable
 spanning-tree portfast
 storm-control broadcast level 5.00
 storm-control multicast level 5.00
 storm-control action shutdown

! Verify
! show spanning-tree root
! show udld
! show storm-control broadcast
